**BCD is in alpha:** an early stage of development, before beta. Many games run, many do not yet, and things can break between builds. When a game fails, please send a log.

> **Tried a game on an earlier build? Reset its settings first.** On the game's page: **Options › Recommended settings › Reset to Recommended**, then check that **Options › Auto-tune › Auto-tune this game** is on.

## iPhone Duo is supported

- **BCD fills both displays.** BCD is now built with the iOS 27 SDK, so installed directly it fills the whole inner display, open or half open, and the outer display when the phone is closed. Until now it got a small window on the inner display unless it ran inside LiveContainer.
- **The interface fits every pose.** On the outer display in landscape, and on the inner display held upright, the top bar was wider than the screen and the Settings button ran off the edge. Now the bar measures itself: when it does not fit, the update chip says **Update** and the memory and controller chips step aside. Upright, the outer display's tab bar now reaches past the camera column. A bar that fits is exactly as before, on every iPhone and iPad.
- **Duo enhancements** (**Settings › Graphics › Foldable iPhone**, experimental, off by default): the **Update available** button could hardly be read in the system's glass. It is clear now.
- Checked screen by screen, open, half open and closed, in landscape and upright, in Apple's iPhone Duo simulator. Games already ran on iPhone Duo; tell us how this build plays on yours, and send a log if anything looks wrong.

## Steam in BCD Dock

- **Steam no longer stays on "connecting".** Steam's client in BCD Dock contacts Steam's crash report server at every start, and one of that server's addresses stopped answering: a Dock start could wait on "connecting" for minutes, or never sign in. BCD now refuses that one server name (BCD sends Steam no crash dumps anyway), so Steam signs in and the game starts. `env.MADEIRA_DNS_REFUSE_CRASH = 0` restores the old lookup.
- **Steam components are not started as games.** Play on **Steamworks Common Redistributables** or **EA app Installer**, which Steam lists with the games, now says that it is a Steam component and that you should start the game itself, instead of opening Steam's own error or waiting five minutes.
- **"Steam is still preparing this game's program"** appears on the starting screen after 20 seconds instead of 60, so you know to keep BCD open.

## External drives on iOS 26

- **Add a drive or folder now opens on iOS 26 and earlier.** On those versions the folder picker in **Settings › Storage › External drives** never appeared: the button did nothing. It is now the system's folder picker presented directly; the folder is still used in place, never copied. **Reconnect** uses the same picker.
- **Windows prefix › Import an export** had the same problem on iOS 26 and earlier and now opens too.

## New

- **Unity games that need Windows Runtime types start without a setting.** Before a start BCD reads the game's own 64-bit programs and libraries, and when one of them needs the Windows Runtime buffer interface (many Unity games: Car For Sale Simulator 2023, Tears of Metal, Turbo Dismount 2, The Long Dark, The Phantom ...), the session gets Wine's Windows Runtime types library. Until now such a game closed at once with a missing-library error (c0000135) unless its settings had `env.MADEIRA_WINTYPES = 1`. A game's own `env.MADEIRA_WINTYPES = 0` keeps it off.
- **Large games with a fixed-address program start the first time.** BCD now measures the window such a program needs from the game's folder before every start, from the library as from BCD Dock (`exe-window-auto`, on by default; `exe-window-auto = 0` in a game's settings turns it off). Until now a game like Persona 5 Royal, Far Cry Primal, Mega Man Battle Network Legacy Collection or Demon Slayer -Kimetsu no Yaiba- The Hinokami Chronicles 2 failed its first start with c0000018 and needed auto-tune's second try.
- **Auto-tune suggests a setting to a game that plays, but slowly.** Until now auto-tune only acted after a game failed. When a game played but its .NET, Mono or Java runtime kept BCD busy with tens of thousands of slow memory writes a second, or its sound was scratchy for the first 20 seconds, auto-tune now suggests the one setting that changes it after the session. You choose **Try it next start**, **Not now** or **Stop for this game**. Nothing changes without your yes. If the game does not play better with the setting, auto-tune takes it back and the game is as it was. The game's page keeps a suggestion you put off.
- **OpenGL and Vulkan tests in the Start menu.** Next to the DirectX tests, **Start › BCD Tests** now has an OpenGL test and a Vulkan test, each in 64-bit and 32-bit: a spinning textured cube with a PASS or FAIL verdict in the title and in the log. OpenGL and Vulkan are per-session settings; with them off, the test says where to turn them on (the Windows desktop's **Options › Direct3D**).
- **Recommended settings reach more Steam games.** A game whose recommended settings were known only by its program name now gets them when it is started from the Steam library or BCD Dock too (BCD looks for the program in the game's folder).
- **Tap to hold** (touch controls editor, for each control): one tap holds a key, mouse or controller button, the next tap lets go.
- **Native ARM64 Windows programs** outside the Windows folder now run on BCD's ARM64 core.
- **LuaJIT with C-style comments:** `env.MADEIRA_LUAJIT_C_COMMENTS = 1` gives a 64-bit game whose own Lua is written with `/* */` and `//` comments a LuaJIT that reads them, for libraries that need memory below 2 GB. Grim Dawn's recommended settings start its compatibility build with it.
- **Compressed textures on iPhones without block-compression support (experimental):** on A13 to A16 iPhones every block-compressed texture is expanded to four to eight times its size, and games that load many of them are closed by iOS. With `env.MADEIRA_MIP_CLAMP_AUTO = 2`, a 64-bit Direct3D 11 game on such an iPhone that comes within 1.5 GB of its memory limit gets its single-level compressed textures at half their width and height, and the largest level of compressed textures from 256 px dropped (value 1 starts at 1,024 px and never shrinks a single-level texture). Such textures look blurrier. For this BCD runs its own build of Direct3D 11, and only on those iPhones: a device that reads compressed textures keeps the usual one, where value 2 works exactly like value 1, and a device with room is untouched. Schedule I, and Shroom and Gloom and Nunholy on devices with less than 12 GB, get it in their recommended settings, and auto-tune tries it after the existing texture clamp. Not confirmed on a device yet.
- **KosmicKrisp (`vulkan = kosmickrisp`) survives a lost shader compiler:** when iOS ends the Metal compiler service under memory pressure, a shader compile is retried instead of failing the game (Enshrouded); at most four compiles run at once, and the shader cache may grow to 4 GB.
- **A second, patched MoltenVK (experimental):** `vulkan = moltenvk-patched` (a line in the game's settings; on devices with KosmicKrisp, the game page's Vulkan choice also offers **MoltenVK (patched)**) runs a newer MoltenVK with tessellation, barrier and indirect-draw changes made for Enshrouded; such a game's OpenGL uses it too. `vulkan = moltenvk` and OpenGL games keep the MoltenVK they had.
- **Unity games on devices with little address space (experimental):** on iPhones and iPads that leave BCD only 4 to 5 GB of free address space, after such a stop auto-tune tries a mode that fits up to 16 of a Unity game's 511 MB blocks of address space (`env.MADEIRA_UNITY_SMALL_VA = 1`). Games that ask for more blocks still stop.
- **KosmicKrisp gets twelve more fixes:** an instance with no layers (OpenGL on KosmicKrisp needs it), border colours for OpenGL, undefined images in shaders, pipeline-statistics queries, 8-sample pipelines on 4-sample devices, a shader operation Metal rejected, timestamp fences, texel buffer views without a format, draws the geometry heap has no room for, and three smaller fixes.
- **A missing library next to the program (experimental):** `env.MADEIRA_IMPORT_APPDIR = 1` makes Windows' loader look in the program's own folder once more for a library a plug-in module needs (Doki Doki Literature Club's recommended settings turn it on); every such miss is named in the log.
- **Faster calls into Direct3D 11 and other system libraries (experimental):** `env.MADEIRA_FEX_EC_EXIT_POOL = 1` in a game's settings lets the emulator skip a table search on calls through the method tables of Direct3D 11, DXGI, XAudio2 and other system objects. Without it that search took up to half of a 64-bit Direct3D 11 game's render thread. Every call gives the same result. Off by default until it is measured on devices: try it in a 64-bit game that is held back by its processor, and send a log with and without it.
- **Clearer warnings on a game's page:** a Red Dead Redemption 2 copy that lacks NvLowLatencyVk.dll (a small file of the game beside RDR2.exe) says the copy is incomplete instead of ending with a missing-library error, and Unity games on devices that leave BCD only about 5 GB of address space say they probably cannot start there.

## Faster

- **Placing memory:** the free-address scan no longer tries addresses above the top of the app's address map. On installs without the extended address space, and on some 3 to 6 GB devices, a failed placement spent most of its time there (`env.MADEIRA_VA_SCAN_CEILING = 0` restores the old scan).
- **Starting large games:** when a game's program files are prepared in memory, values that cannot point into them are no longer looked up. This saves up to 10 seconds at the start of large games (`env.MADEIRA_IAT_SYNC_SPAN = 0` restores the old lookup).
- **Folder listings in Windows:** a file's extended attributes are listed once instead of twice, so Steam's folder scans while it prepares a game run up to about a quarter faster (`env.MADEIRA_XATTR_ONE_LIST = 0` restores the old reads).

## Fixes and improvements

- **OpenGL games:** a graphics call could reach BCD's OpenGL layer without its thread information when iOS interrupted it at one exact point; the game then crashed or misbehaved minutes later (Alien Tenant, Buckshot Roulette, Mewgenics and other OpenGL games). That step is now checked and repeated when it happens.
- **Memory:** a program's code copies are dropped together with the memory it releases, so a new allocation at the same address no longer has its writes sent to the old copy (games that free and reserve the same region again: Ratchet & Clank: Rift Apart, the EA app, Battlefield 2 with dgVoodoo, Requiem with a Glide wrapper). `env.MADEIRA_ALIAS_RELEASE = 0` restores the old behaviour; `= 1` also zeroes each copy when the memory is decommitted.
- **Crashes fixed:**
  - a game's main thread no longer dies a few seconds in when a program image it had copied was unmapped (Hellblade II: Senua's Saga, Red Dead Redemption 2, the EA app);
  - a thread ending in a 32-bit program no longer reads a torn-down thread block (Far Cry 3 and others);
  - Direct3D 12 root signatures with up to 64 parameters (was 32; Mechstermination Force);
  - a program that changes a page's protection while its out-parameter lies on that page (FTL, Peggle Deluxe);
  - DirectInput callbacks written with the C calling convention no longer break the program's stack (The Wolf Among Us);
  - Quantum Break and other 64-bit programs that start `cmd.exe` get a 64-bit command prompt.
- **Sound:** the XAudio2 callback-order fix now actually ships in BCD's XAudio2 libraries, so auto-tune's line for a game that crashed on its first sound callbacks (The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim, about 30 seconds in) takes effect.
- **Memory:**
  - the free-address scan starts at the lowest address iOS maps for the app, so placing a small block no longer tries tens of thousands of refused addresses first (`env.MADEIRA_VA_SCAN_FLOOR = 0` restores the old scan);
  - a game whose large program BCD must place at a fixed address (Hogwarts Legacy) gets the free part of that range when iOS put something small inside it, instead of stopping.
- **32-bit programs:**
  - a 32-bit game started together with Windows' services (PES 2017, Phantasy Star Online Blue Burst) can reach Windows' GDI table;
  - a failed setup of a 32-bit process ends only that process;
  - Windows' DEP options are given to a 32-bit caller only;
  - `env.MADEIRA_WOW_JUMBO_INSIDE = 2` places a program's 1 GB reserve inside its own window again (The Binding of Isaac);
  - a crash report now also says where the faulting address came from.
- **BCD Dock:**
  - a game's one-time installs run for a Steam library on an external drive too;
  - when Steam's sign-in gets no answer for 45 seconds, the starting screen says that the connection to Steam's servers is slow or blocked;
  - a session ends when the game's Steam host crashes at shutdown or when the game starts its crash uploader and ends (Enshrouded, Exo7, Dressmaker), instead of waiting;
  - Steam is no longer started offline while the JIT shortcut briefly holds cellular data off;
  - clearer messages when Steam's client cannot reach Valve's servers and when there is no saved sign-in for an offline start.
- **Epic:**
  - the Rockstar launcher of an Epic game (GTA V Enhanced) runs in the Windows desktop, where the Windows services it needs run (`env.BCD_EPIC_SERVICES_DESKTOP = 0` keeps the direct start);
  - Epic's older JSON build manifests are read (Bus Simulator 21);
  - the end-of-session message no longer says the host stopped when it never ran.
- **EA:** Need for Speed: Most Wanted (2012) from Steam gets Windows' service manager and the EA app's libraries in its recommended settings, for EA's launcher that asks to enable background services (not confirmed on a device yet).
- **Background:** a KosmicKrisp game (Metal 4) is held in the background like the others.
- **Steam sign-in:** a network error while Steam waits for your approval on the Steam app no longer ends the sign-in; BCD waits and asks again.
- **Direct3D 12:**
  - a released texture is kept until the GPU has finished with it. Mina the Hollower, Ghost of Tsushima and skate. ended when the GPU still used a texture the game had released (`tex-defer = 0` restores the old behaviour);
  - a copy between an uncompressed texture and a block-compressed one now works (`t2t-reinterp = 0` turns it off).
- **A 64-bit program that writes into its own memory through Windows** (Trackmania): with `env.MADEIRA_SELF_WRITE = 1`, `env.MADEIRA_SELF_WRITE_PRIVATE = 1` also covers its own allocations.
- **Windows' non-blocking overlapped I/O polls** (opt-in): `env.MADEIRA_OVERLAPPED_SYSTEM_APC = 1` lets such a poll finish its I/O, plus `kernelbase` in `env.MADEIRA_OPTIN_DLLS` for a 64-bit program (Trackmania's recommended settings set both).
- **Optional Windows DLLs:** `mscms` can be added to `env.MADEIRA_OPTIN_DLLS` (Adobe AIR games such as Brawlhalla).
- **Steam:**
  - Trackmania's required Ubisoft Connect files are downloaded with the game (other shared install files are still left out);
  - downloads keep a content server in rotation until it fails three times (`env.MADEIRA_STEAM_CDN_ROTATE = 0` restores the old order);
  - a Steam Cloud file whose download was cut short is fetched once more;
  - files Steam packs as zlib, gzip or raw deflate are read;
  - a file that does not check out is named in the log with what arrived.
- **Epic and EA:** repairing a large game no longer lets memory grow until iOS closes BCD.
- **Send Log:** a log sent after updating BCD is filed under the build that wrote it, not under the build that sent it.
- **Messages name the right screens:**
  - **Settings › Visual C++ runtime**, **Settings › Memory & performance** and **Settings › BCD Dock**;
  - a Windows desktop that is still running points to **Open** on Home's Windows desktop card.
- **Logs:**
  - a settings line written without `env.` (for example `MADEIRA_X = 1`) is named in the log, since nothing reads it;
  - the time BCD's fault handler spends on emulated writes is measured correctly again: it was cut to 32 bits.
- **Auto-tune:**
  - a game iOS closes at 95 % of its memory limit, or after one or two freezes right at the limit, now counts as closed for memory, so auto-tune tries the swap file for it (DRAGON BALL Sparking! ZERO, DummyWar); before, it tried nothing;
  - a game that closed by itself before showing a picture is no longer written off when you then leave the app, so its fix is tried (The Binding of Isaac);
  - on a phone that gives apps about 4 GB, the message after a memory stop with nothing left to try names the class of device the game needs;
  - a 6 GB phone's memory stop in a Direct3D 12 game is no longer blamed on graphics memory;
  - about 120 new or corrected rules from players' logs, among them:
    - Vulkan games that need KosmicKrisp;
    - Keen engine games;
    - Unity games on devices with little address space;
    - 32-bit games on 454 GB address maps;
    - Baldur's Gate II: Enhanced Edition's OpenGL;
    - Days Gone's spatial audio;
    - HITMAN World of Assassination's address reserve;
    - Doki Doki Literature Club's libraries;
    - a Steam client too old for a game's Steam library, and the memory the Steam client itself needs on 6 GB phones;
    - PlayStation 4 programs;
    - a Godot OpenGL test that waits for ever;
    - Trackmania's missing Ubisoft Connect files;
    - Grand Theft Auto IV's 32-bit window;
    - Digimon Story Time Stranger's address reserve;
    - Unreal Engine 5 reserves served in part;
    - a mod updater's dialog that stays open;
    - Steam's sign-in waiting on the crash report server;
    - Media Foundation games that need MFPlay (Disney Speedstorm) or the video processor (Devil May Cry HD Collection);
    - 64-bit Epic games whose sign-in host never reported (Windbound, Frostpunk);
    - NW.js games whose renderer crashed (an experiment);
    - Direct3D 8 games without OpenGL (Thief: Deadly Shadows);
    - a 64-bit Direct3D 9 game that quits without a message (Euro Truck Simulator 2: BCD's own Direct3D 9);
    - a self-modifying start-up check (Persona 3 Reload Demo, Yakuza: Like a Dragon);
    - Cyberpunk 2077's 64 GB reserve;
    - compressed textures that stay too large after the texture clamp;
    - EA's launcher started outside BCD Dock;
    - a game's own hardware check (Red Dead Redemption 2: answer Yes) and video-memory check (FINAL FANTASY XIII);
    - games that need NVIDIA PhysX (**Start › BCD Runtimes › PhysX**) or Direct3D 12 feature level 12_1 (FINAL FANTASY TACTICS - The Ivalice Chronicles);
  - Play waits up to 30 seconds for the verdict of a run iOS ended, and the on-device log scan is faster;
  - corrections: an OpenGL ES session's BCD Dock host and Battle.net's setup after its own error screen get their advice;
  - a setting that passed a game's own AVX check is kept;
  - after a BGFX game fails to get an OpenGL context, auto-tune tries Desktop OpenGL;
  - its advice for a game that misses a Steam interface names the SteamOS/Linux compatibility option, and it reads only the current launch.

## Games

- **New recommended settings:**
  - Action and adventure: The Plucky Squire, HITMAN World of Assassination, Legacy of Kain Soul Reaver 1&2 Remastered, Alice: Madness Returns, Dead Rising 2, Sleeping Dogs, Days Gone, Darwin's Paradox!, The Coffin of Andy and Leyley, Assassin's Creed Mirage, Far Cry Primal, Devil May Cry HD Collection, Thief: Deadly Shadows, Demon Slayer -Kimetsu no Yaiba- The Hinokami Chronicles 2, The Phantom.
  - RPG: FINAL FANTASY XIII, Baldur's Gate II: Enhanced Edition, Game of Thrones: Kingsroad, Digimon Story Time Stranger, ONE PIECE: PIRATE WARRIORS 3, Persona 5 Royal, Mega Man Battle Network Legacy Collection Vol. 1.
  - Survival, building and simulation: Enshrouded, The Sims Legacy Collection, Jurassic World Evolution, The Long Dark, Slime Rancher, Frostpunk (Epic Games Store), Windbound (Epic Games Store), Car For Sale Simulator 2023.
  - Racing, shooting and fighting: Trackmania, OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast, Ground Branch, Brawlhalla, Disney Speedstorm, Turbo Dismount 2.
  - Indie: CatMailCo, One More Lawn, Vampire Crawlers, FUMES, Dumpster Gang, Tears of Metal, Snapshot!, Nunholy.
  - Visual novel: Nora to Oujo to Noraneko Heart (ノラと皇女と野良猫ハート).
- **Updated:**
  - Rockstar: Grand Theft Auto IV: The Complete Edition, Grand Theft Auto III.
  - Big releases: Hogwarts Legacy, The Last of Us Part I, Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered, METAL GEAR SOLID V: THE PHANTOM PAIN, Persona 3 Reload, Yakuza: Like a Dragon.
  - Far Cry 3 (Steam and other copies), Euro Truck Simulator 2, The Elder Scrolls IV: Oblivion, S.T.A.L.K.E.R. (X-Ray engine games).
  - FINAL FANTASY TACTICS - The Ivalice Chronicles, FINAL FANTASY RESONANCE, Zenless Zone Zero, DRAGON BALL FighterZ.
  - REPLACED, REANIMAL, Cult of the Lamb, Unrailed! 2: Back on Track, Doki Doki Literature Club, The Wolf Among Us Remastered, The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth, STAR WARS Galactic Racer, Quaver, Anodyne.
  - Need for Speed: Most Wanted (2012), Outlast (the DRM-free copy's launcher), Schedule I, Shroom and Gloom.
  - Half-Life and the other GoldSrc games (Desktop OpenGL).

## Known issues

- **Call of Duty: Infinite Warfare** reserves more address space than any iPhone or iPad gives and stops early. No setting changes this yet.
- **Football Manager 27** stops within the first minute of play on every device. No setting changes this yet.
- **Heavy games after a few minutes:** iOS lowers the processor clock after a few minutes of heavy play, even when the phone is not hot.

Install help, game reports and ideas: the BCD-Games Discord is open, https://discord.gg/43TmupTVug
